  "moments": [
    {
      "id": "primera-victoria",
      "title": {
        "es": "Primera victoria",
        "en": "First win"
      },
      "text": {
        "es": "Tras unas tablas en la primera partida, Alekhine ganó la segunda y la cuarta con blancas.",
        "en": "After a draw in game 1, Alekhine won games 2 and 4 with White."
      },
      "round": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "dos-de-bogoljubov",
      "title": {
        "es": "Bogoljubov reacciona tarde",
        "en": "Bogoljubov hits back too late"
      },
      "text": {
        "es": "Bogoljubov ganó dos partidas seguidas, la 23 y la 24, pero ya estaba demasiado lejos en el marcador.",
        "en": "Bogoljubov won two games in a row, 23 and 24, but by then he was too far behind."
      },
      "round": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "mas-de-quince",
      "title": {
        "es": "Pasar de 15 puntos",
        "en": "Getting past 15 points"
      },
      "text": {
        "es": "Alekhine tenía seis victorias desde la partida 17, pero necesitaba más de 15 puntos: llegó a 15 con su triunfo en la 25 y los superó con las tablas de la 26.",
        "en": "Alekhine had six wins from game 17 on, but needed more than 15 points: he reached 15 with his win in game 25 and passed it with a draw in game 26."
      },
      "round": 26
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Comentando una de las partidas en su libro de mejores partidas, Alekhine escribió: «Esta partida, más que ninguna otra, demuestra lo inútil que fue, desde el punto de vista deportivo, organizar este segundo match».",
        "en": "Annotating one of the games in his best-games collection, Alekhine wrote: \"This game – more than any other – proves how useless from the sporting point of view was the arrangement of this second match.\""
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "Wikipedia",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Chess_Championship_1934"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Como en 1929, ganaba el primero que sumara seis victorias y más de 15 puntos.",
        "en": "As in 1929, the winner was the first to collect six wins and more than 15 points."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "Wikipedia",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Chess_Championship_1934"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Se jugó en doce ciudades de Alemania, empezando en Baden-Baden y terminando en Berlín.",
        "en": "It was played in twelve German cities, starting in Baden-Baden and finishing in Berlin."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "OlimpBase",
        "url": "https://www.olimpbase.org/ind-wcc/wc1934-wch.html"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": {
        "es": "Era la segunda vez que se enfrentaban por el título: en 1929, en la única defensa previa de Alekhine, ya le había ganado 15½ a 9½.",
        "en": "It was their second title match: in 1929, Alekhine's only previous defence, he had already beaten Bogoljubov 15½–9½."
      },
      "source": {
        "label": "Wikipedia",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Chess_Championship_1934"
      }
    }
  ],
